course: dictionary
lesson: 15246
title: Words that paint light
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words let you see a scene in your mind. «Shimmer» is one of them. When you read «The lake shimmered in the moonlight», you can almost see the soft light moving on the water. Writers choose words like this to make a place feel calm or magical.
explain: Look at the words around «shimmer» to work out its meaning. The lake is in moonlight, and the light seems to move a little. So shimmer means to shine with a soft, wavering light. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «The lake shone with a soft, wavering light in the moonlight» still makes sense.
explain: «Shimmer» can also be a noun, a thing you can name: «The shimmer of the silk dress caught her eye.» Here the shimmer is the soft shine on the dress. A word can be a verb in one sentence and a noun in another, so always check how it is used.
fact: To shimmer is to shine with a soft light that seems to move or shake a little, like light on water.
fact: A shimmer is a soft, wavering shine.
fact: «Shimmering» describes something that is shining softly and moving a little, such as a shimmering lake.
fact: In very hot weather, the air above a road can seem to shimmer, because hot air bends the light.
fact: «A shimmer of hope» means a small bit of hope.
exercise: «The lake shimmered in the moonlight.» What does shimmered mean? | *Shone with a soft, wavering light | Froze solid in the cold | Made a loud splashing sound | Became very deep and dark
exercise: «The road shimmered in the summer heat.» Why might a road look like it is shimmering? | The road is wet with rain | *Hot air bends the light | The road is covered in snow | Someone painted it silver
exercise: «The shimmer of the silk dress caught her eye.» Find and copy the noun. | silk | eye | caught | *shimmer
test: «A shimmer of hope rose in his heart when the rescue boat appeared.» What does a shimmer of hope mean? | A heavy weight of sadness | A huge storm of worry | A loud shout for help | *A small bit of hope
test: «The stars shimmered over the quiet sea.» Which word means shone softly? | quiet | stars | over | *shimmered
exam: «Stories say the magic cave floor shimmered, and Mia stepped in carefully.» What does shimmered suggest? | It was covered in mud | It was very loud | *It shone with a soft, moving light | It was cold and wet
